## 9. Core Product Components

## 9.1 `.x3` Language

The `.x3` language is the main developer interface.

It must support:

```text
intent declarations
asset references
chain references
VM references
contract/program/module declarations
typed calls
route policies
risk policies
proof requirements
finality requirements
refund policies
timeout rules
solver policies
relayer quorum
RPC quorum
invariants
error handling
test declarations
```

Example:

```x3
intent deep_cross_vm_swap {
  from arbitrum.USDC amount 500
  to solana.SOL receiver user.wallet

  route best_score {
    weight safety 50
    weight price 25
    weight speed 15
    weight fee 10
  }

  require slippage <= 0.5%
  require route_score >= 90
  require source_finality >= safe
  require destination_finality >= confirmed
  require refund_to == user.wallet

  on timeout refund
  on solver_fail refund_and_slash
  on proof_conflict dispute

  invariant no_double_claim
  invariant no_double_refund
  invariant no_claim_after_refund
  invariant no_refund_after_claim
}
```

---

## 9.2 X3 Compiler

The compiler converts `.x3` files into deterministic execution plans.

Compiler pipeline:

```text
.x3 source
  ↓
lexer
  ↓
parser
  ↓
AST
  ↓
static analyzer
  ↓
X3IR
  ↓
route plan
  ↓
VM-specific execution plans
```

The compiler must produce:

```text
intent_hash
route_hash
X3IR
VM call plans
proof requirements
refund rules
risk score
test plan
mainnet safety report
```

Mainnet mode must reject:

```text
missing refund path
missing proof requirements
missing finality policy
single RPC trust
single relayer trust
mock adapters
stub execution
unknown assets
unsafe slippage
unbounded deadline
unverified contract calls
unlimited token approvals
manual-only recovery
```

---

## 9.3 X3IR

`X3IR` is the internal representation of every compiled `.x3` file.

It must include:

```text
intent_hash
route_hash
source asset
destination asset
amount
receiver
chains
VMs
contracts/programs/modules
typed calls
constraints
proof requirements
finality requirements
timeouts
refund rules
solver rules
relayer rules
RPC quorum rules
risk policy
state machine transitions
invariants
post-conditions
```

`X3IR` must be deterministic. The same `.x3` file must always produce the same canonical intent hash.

---

## 9.4 Universal Contract Linker

The Contract Linker connects X3-lang to existing smart contracts, programs, modules, and schemas.

Supported connector types:

```text
EVM ABI
Solana IDL
Move module ABI
CosmWasm schema
Substrate metadata
Cairo ABI
Bitcoin script template
TON ABI
```

Example EVM contract declaration:

```x3
contract uniswap_v3 on arbitrum {
  vm evm
  address 0xE592427A0AEce92De3Edee1F18E0157C05861564
  abi "@x3/abis/uniswap_v3_swap_router"
}
```

Example Solana program declaration:

```x3
program jupiter on solana {
  vm svm
  id JUP6LkbZbjS1jKKwapdHNy74zcZ3tLUZoi5QNyVTaV4
  idl "@x3/idls/jupiter"
}
```

Example Move module declaration:

```x3
module cetus_swap on sui {
  vm move
  package 0x...
  module router
  abi "@x3/move/cetus"
}
```

The linker must validate:

```text
method exists
argument names are valid
argument types match
asset chain matches contract chain
approval is bounded
target address/program/module is known
risk profile exists
receipt decoder exists
failure path exists
proof requirements exist
```

---

## 9.5 Typed Call Blocks

X3-lang must support typed calls into linked contracts.

Example:

```x3
call uniswap_v3.exactInputSingle {
  tokenIn arbitrum.USDC
  tokenOut arbitrum.WETH
  fee 500
  recipient x3.executor
  amountIn 500
  amountOutMinimum auto
}
```

Each call compiles to an internal object:

```text
X3ContractCall {
  vm_type
  chain_id
  target
  method
  encoded_args
  value
  gas_budget
  proof_required
  rollback_policy
}
```

VM adapters then convert `X3ContractCall` into native execution:

```text
EVM calldata
SVM instruction set
Move transaction block
CosmWasm execute msg
Substrate extrinsic
Cairo calldata
Bitcoin script
TON message
```

---

## 9.6 Post-Conditions

Every production call must support post-condition checks.

Example:

```x3
after call {
  require balance(user, solana.SOL) >= quoted_min
  require spent(arbitrum.USDC) <= 500
  require no_unapproved_spender
  prove receipt
  prove event
}
```

Post-conditions protect users from unexpected execution results.

Required post-condition types:

```text
balance check
spent amount check
received amount check
slippage check
event check
receipt check
spender check
approval check
state transition check
```

---

## 9.7 Approval Policy

X3-lang must prevent unsafe token approval behavior.

Example:

```x3
approval_policy strict {
  approve_exact_amount true
  revoke_after true
  deny_unlimited_approval true
  spender_must_equal contract.address
}
```

Mainnet mode must reject unlimited approvals unless explicitly allowed by a dangerous override flag.

