## 9.11 Atomic State Machine

Every intent must follow a deterministic state machine.

Required states:

```text
CREATED
COMPILED
VALIDATED
QUOTED
ROUTE_SELECTED
SOURCE_LOCKED
SOURCE_FINALIZED
DESTINATION_FILLED
DESTINATION_FINALIZED
SOURCE_CLAIMED
COMPLETED
REFUND_REQUESTED
REFUNDED
FAILED
DISPUTED
SLASHED
```

Required guarantees:

```text
No double claim.
No double refund.
No claim after refund.
No refund after claim.
No route mutation after source lock.
No destination fill without source lock.
No source claim without destination fill proof.
No state transition without required proof.
No lock without known refund path.
```

---

## 9.12 HTLC Atomicity

X3 must support HTLC-based atomic execution.

Required HTLC features:

```text
hashlock generation
preimage reveal
source lock
destination fill
claim path
refund path
expiry validation
replay protection
double-claim prevention
double-refund prevention
secret reuse detection
```

Example:

```x3
atomic htlc {
  hashlock sha256(preimage)
  source_timeout 30m
  destination_timeout 15m
  refund_after source_timeout
  reveal_preimage only_on_claim
}
```

