## 9.14 Solver Marketplace

Solvers compete to fulfill user intents.

Solver bid must include:

```text
solver ID
route
price
fee
deadline
bond
source asset
destination asset
expected output
liquidity source
finality estimate
risk score
signature
```

Required solver rules:

```text
solver registration
solver bonding
signed bids
route commitment
fill proof submission
claim authorization
solver reputation score
slashing for failure
slashing for fake fill
slashing for route substitution
```

Example:

```x3
solver_market {
  mode competitive
  min_reputation 95
  min_bond 10000 X3
  max_fee 0.3%
  require signed_bid
  require route_commitment
  slash_on failure
  slash_on fake_fill
}
```

---

## 9.15 Relayer Swarm

Relayers monitor chains and submit proofs.

Required relayer features:

```text
relayer registration
relayer bonding
event watching
proof submission
multi-relayer quorum
duplicate proof handling
conflicting proof detection
bad proof rejection
relayer health scoring
slashing for false proof
backup relayers
watchtower mode
```

Example:

```x3
relayers {
  quorum 3_of_5
  min_reputation 90
  require independent_rpc true
  slash_on false_proof
  rotate every 100 intents
}
```

---

## 9.16 RPC Quorum

X3 must never rely on a single RPC in production mode.

Required checks:

```text
block hash agreement
receipt agreement
event agreement
balance agreement
slot/block height agreement
finality agreement
latency score
error score
fork detection
auto-disable bad RPC
```

Example:

```x3
rpc_quorum {
  source require 2_of_3
  destination require 3_of_5
  reject if receipt_disagree
  reject if finality_disagree
}
```

---

## 9.17 Finality Oracle

Every VM has different finality rules. X3 must make them explicit.

Required finality support:

```text
EVM safe/finalized
L2 challenge/finality model
Solana processed/confirmed/finalized
MoveVM checkpoint/certified finality
Cosmos/Tendermint finality
Substrate GRANDPA finality
Bitcoin confirmation depth
Cairo/Starknet finality
TON finality model
```

Example:

```x3
finality_policy strict {
  evm require finalized
  svm require confirmed
  bitcoin require confirmations >= 6
  move require checkpoint_certified
}
```

---

## 9.18 Timeout and Refund Engine

Refunds are a first-class feature.

Required refund features:

```text
source timeout
destination timeout
solver timeout
relayer timeout
grace window
auto-refund builder
refund proof
refund dashboard
expiring-lock monitor
third-party keeper refund
refund gas policy
partial refund
full refund
```

Example:

```x3
refund_policy user_safe {
  refund_to user.wallet
  refund_after 30m
  allow_third_party_refund true
  refund_gas_payer solver
}
```

Required guarantee:

```text
Every lock must have a known refund path before execution.
```

