## 16. Security Requirements

The system must enforce these invariants:

```text
No double claim.
No double refund.
No claim after refund.
No refund after claim.
No route mutation after lock.
No destination fill without source lock.
No source claim without destination proof.
No timeout bypass.
No stale finality proof.
No forged relayer quorum.
No invalid VM adapter receipt.
No solver claim without committed bid.
No unsafe unlimited approval.
No production execution through mock adapter.
No production proof from simulation only.
```

---

## 17. Privacy and MEV Protection

X3 must support privacy features designed for user protection and MEV resistance.

Allowed privacy features:

```text
private routing
commit-reveal
encrypted solver bids
private mempool preference
delayed route reveal
minimal public metadata
preimage secrecy until claim
sandwich prevention
```

Disallowed use cases:

```text
hiding theft
evading sanctions
obfuscating stolen funds
bypassing compliance controls
laundering assets
```

Example:

```x3
privacy {
  use_commit_reveal true
  private_mempool preferred
  encrypt_solver_bids true
  prevent_sandwich true
}
```

