## 20. Major Risks

### Risk 1: Scope Explosion

Trying to build a full smart contract language too early would slow the project down.

Mitigation:

```text
X3-lang v1 connects smart contracts.
It does not replace smart contract languages.
```

### Risk 2: Cross-VM Complexity

Every VM has different execution, finality, and receipt models.

Mitigation:

```text
Start with EVM ↔ SVM only.
Expand VM support after proof ledger and refund engine work.
```

### Risk 3: AI Unsafe Execution

AI may generate dangerous or invalid actions.

Mitigation:

```text
AI drafts only.
Compiler verifies.
User signs.
Mainnet gate blocks unsafe execution.
```

### Risk 4: Fake Progress

Agents may update docs or scoreboard numbers without implementing real code.

Mitigation:

```text
Scoreboard must link to tests, proofs, logs, chain evidence, and CI results.
Mainnet release gate must detect mocks, stubs, fake paths, and missing proof.
```

### Risk 5: Bridge/Protocol Dependency

External protocols may fail or change.

Mitigation:

```text
Treat bridges and aggregators as replaceable route modules.
X3 owns proof, risk, refund, and route scoring.
```

