## 22. Final Acceptance Definition

X3-lang is considered successful when this complete flow works:

```text
User gives plain English request.
AI drafts .x3 intent.
Compiler validates .x3 file.
X3IR is generated.
Route engine scores routes.
Solver bids.
User signs.
Source VM locks funds.
Relayer swarm proves lock.
Finality oracle confirms source.
Destination VM fills.
Relayer swarm proves fill.
Finality oracle confirms destination.
Source VM claim executes.
Proof ledger records everything.
Scoreboard updates automatically.
If anything fails, refund executes.
If anyone lies, slashing triggers.
Explorer shows the full lifecycle.
```

The product is not considered complete when documentation claims features exist.

The product is complete only when tests, proofs, logs, adapters, and chain evidence prove the features work.

